WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.920
You know how it is. We put up a community post,&nbsp;
asking for our esteemed audience’s opinion on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.200
given anomalous topic, and when you give us the&nbsp;
answers, we make a video like this, responding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:18.400
to them. It’s a perfect system - It runs like&nbsp;
Clockwork. Or, more specifically, like SCP-914,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.760
The Clockworks - a fascinating safe-class anomaly&nbsp;
that can transform anything placed inside one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:29.600
its chambers in a number of exciting - and&nbsp;
sometimes terrifying - ways. We asked you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.640
if the device was in your&nbsp;
hands, how would you use it?

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.280
And before we get into some of the great answers&nbsp;
we selected, here’s a quick refresher on how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.360
the machine works. When an object or entity is&nbsp;
placed into its first chamber, the user has the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:49.120
option to select one of five settings, each of&nbsp;
which leads to a relatively predictable result.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.160
First, Rough, which completely destroys the item,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.840
often utterly disintegrating it and turning it&nbsp;
into dust. There is no way to repair such an item.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.600
Coarse is a little less severe.&nbsp;
It dismantles the object rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.320
than destroys, cleanly and efficiently&nbsp;
breaking it into its component parts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.320
often in a manner that would be&nbsp;
conducive to the object’s reconstruction.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.160
1:1 is a setting that replaces the&nbsp;
object or entity with something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.440
similar, usually in size, weight, or quality.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.960
Fine is a setting that improves&nbsp;
the item within reasonable means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.800
rarely straying into anomalous&nbsp;
territory with these improvements.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.400
And the most mysterious and volatile setting&nbsp;
of all is Very Fine, which improves the item&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.920
or entity in an unpredictable, anomalous&nbsp;
manner, sometimes to disastrous results.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.160
Great, so now we’re all caught up.&nbsp;
We’ve handed you a great power.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.920
Now let’s see if you can handle&nbsp;
it with great responsibility…

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.400
Sam Rosenthal said, “I feel like it would be&nbsp;
interesting to put a musical instrument like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.880
a piano through it on 'very fine.'. It would&nbsp;
be interesting to see what the machine would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.120
consider to be an improvement with something&nbsp;
so subjective. Edit: It would also need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:03.120
be something very high-end, like a Steinway, so&nbsp;
that it didn't just come out as a nicer piano.”

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.360
Putting a Steinway piano into the Clockworks&nbsp;
on the Fine setting would likely result in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:17.120
improvement, making it a finer instrument&nbsp;
with a sweeter, richer sound. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.080
putting it into the machine on the Very Fine&nbsp;
setting would be more likely to make the piano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.320
come alive, turn its legs into limbs&nbsp;
capable of functional locomotion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.240
and as for it’s keys, they kinda&nbsp;
already resemble teeth in a weird way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.480
so we’re going to say that’s a no-brainer.&nbsp;
It’s keys are definitely turning into actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.200
teeth that are dripping with deadly venom.&nbsp;
Anyone else getting Super Mario 64 flashbacks?

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.600
Isaac Ealey said, “If most of the&nbsp;
chains binding SCP-2317 have snapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.800
then presumably there is remnants&nbsp;
of the chains laying around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.080
The foundation could combine this&nbsp;
material with regular chains and put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.840
it on very fine in SCP-914 to create new&nbsp;
ones to restrain the devourer of worlds.”

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.600
Something that’s extremely important to&nbsp;
remember is that the results of a Very Fine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.560
transmutation are always unpredictable.&nbsp;
Upgrading the chains may result in them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.360
literally gaining a mind of their own and&nbsp;
trying to imprison the known universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.200
And if they do simply become better&nbsp;
chains, actually fixing them to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.720
Devourer becomes the next issue. Personally,&nbsp;
you’re welcome to take care of that one first…

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.320
Eddiember said, “So I had a crazy thought. I&nbsp;
would put the Substance Produced by SCP-153&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.800
(the soul extractor) through on 1:1. I'd&nbsp;
be interested to see what the Clockwork&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.120
would quantify as the equivilent to a soul. I&nbsp;
think it would be different depending on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.440
personality of the Soul insert, like while&nbsp;
one person may give their soul for love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.480
another one may give their&nbsp;
soul for a Chocolate Bar.”

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.880
Well, if the scientifically dubious&nbsp;
1907 metaphysical experiments of Duncan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.560
MacDougall are to be believed, souls, despite&nbsp;
being ephemeral, weigh roughly 21 grams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.280
If the Clockworks have a difficult time&nbsp;
qualitatively judging the value of a human soul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.800
perhaps it would provide a vaguely&nbsp;
valuable item that weighs roughly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:06.960
21 grams. Little heartless, sure, but what can&nbsp;
you expect? It’s all cogs, gears, and pulleys.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.320
Shain said, “I would be interested in what&nbsp;
would happen if you took a drawing of Scp-096&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.440
and put it on the 1:1 setting, would it turn&nbsp;
into a realistic photo? And if yes then could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.280
this trigger the shy guy to attack you? I&nbsp;
would also check this the other way around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.320
to see of you could get a pic of Scp-096&nbsp;
that doesn't activate his killing spree.”

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.040
While it’s impossible to know for sure, we&nbsp;
personally wouldn’t risk this one. A single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:37.520
photon of SCP-096’s face is enough to activate its&nbsp;
rage state, as the failure of Dr. Dan’s SCRAMBLE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:43.680
Goggles proved, so even if the Clockworks produces&nbsp;
an even half-decent true representation of 096,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.840
looking at it will give you a&nbsp;
truly horrifying death sentence.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:54.160
Alek B said, “I would actually somehow get a&nbsp;
part of 682's body mass, and experiment on it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.720
Maybe downgrading the 682 piece by piece&nbsp;
wouldn't let it combine together again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.280
or maybe just upgrade, downgrade or&nbsp;
let some parts of 682 as they were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.280
maybe 682 wouldn't be able to adapt&nbsp;
to this. (Not a big chance tho).”

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.040
Anything involving SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy&nbsp;
Reptile, is going to be unpredictable, by the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.880
nature of the cantankerous lizard itself. The big&nbsp;
issue with trying to downgrade 682 piecemeal is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.560
that each part would be likely to reform and adapt&nbsp;
before you had a chance to process the rest of it.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.640
Xwingknight said, “What happens if you put one&nbsp;
pill from SCP-500 on very fine? I would recommend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.520
against any more because they are not many, but&nbsp;
maybe it would duplicate the pill because I don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.160
know how you’d improve it as it already cures&nbsp;
literally anything. Or maybe do it on rough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.400
see if it gets broken down to its components&nbsp;
and see if it can be reverse engineered!”

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:49.920
All we know for sure about SCP-500 and&nbsp;
SCP-914 is that, on the “Fine” setting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:56.320
it results in SCP-427, a locket with rejuvinating&nbsp;
properties. The Foundation are reluctant to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:01.600
any tests on SCP-500 given how valuable&nbsp;
they are and how limited the supply is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.240
but the Very Fine setting could result in&nbsp;
something amazing. Maybe a doctor capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.960
of curing anything - You know, the kind&nbsp;
of doctor that SCP-049 wishes he was.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:17.280
MrArthur said, “It would be interesting to put the&nbsp;
researcher that presents the SCPs on "very fine".&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:22.400
Maybe the machine will make the researcher into&nbsp;
one of the writers of SCP-001 The databases.”

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:33.680
Wait you mean…me?! You want to put ME in that&nbsp;
thing?! Oh you definitely don’t want to put me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.440
in the machine at the Very Fine setting.&nbsp;
We’d suddenly be capable of putting out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:43.200
new video every few minutes. It’d destroy your&nbsp;
timelines. And even if you unsubscribed, you’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:50.400
still see the videos. They’d just keep coming.
There is no escape. SCP Explained is Eternal!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.960 --> 00:07:00.240
There is no escape! There is no escape!…
Dr. Veronica said, “Aaaaah, it happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.920
my request to be hired as a doctor&nbsp;
at the Foundation has been accepted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.600
How about taking SCP-458, the Never-Ending Pizza&nbsp;
Box, and putting it through on Very Fine? I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:14.880
imagine that may be able to turn it into something&nbsp;
that can infinitely reproduce any food you desire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.400
Failing that, maybe put a politician&nbsp;
through on the Very Fine setting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:23.520
Will that make them a very fine politician, or a&nbsp;
very fine person that happens to be a politician?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.800
Or will it make them Senator&nbsp;
Armstrong from Metal Gear Rising?”

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:34.880
Pizzas and politicians, the two Ps of conflicting&nbsp;
emotions. Putting SCP-458 through SCP-914 might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:40.240
result in it turning into an entire pizzeria,&nbsp;
that gives away perfect pizzas at no cost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:44.560
They’ll have wonderful service, impeccable&nbsp;
atmosphere, and always remember your name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.880
They’ll even give away free breadsticks and&nbsp;
exquisite garlic bread bowls for the tables,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.680
along with discounts on the finest mid-tier&nbsp;
wine you’ve ever seen. It’d be divine.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:58.320
The politicians, on the other hand, could&nbsp;
go in one of two ways. Maybe they’d become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.720
a true champion of the people - Guided by&nbsp;
ironclad principles that they’ll fight tooth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:06.880
and nail to see actualized, doing right&nbsp;
by their voters and the general public,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.480
treating their office with dignity&nbsp;
and poise. Or they’ll be the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:14.560
incredible silver-tongued, self-serving,&nbsp;
conniving backstabber you’ve ever seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.080
endlessly devoted to winning office&nbsp;
in order to monetize their position,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.360
raid the country’s coffers, and run off with a fat&nbsp;
bag of swag while the nation burns behind them.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:28.560
Oh wait, you said Very Fine? Chances are they can&nbsp;
shoot lasers and are maybe fifty feet tall, too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.720
That’s just the kind of thing you need to expect.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:39.200
George Simonovich said, “If you put&nbsp;
SCP-1609 through on the fine setting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.760
maybe it would restore it to its chair form.”

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:48.240
That is a possibility, but given the anomalous&nbsp;
nature of SCP-1609 - the vengeful Remains of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:52.880
a Chair - it’s equally possible that it&nbsp;
might just become higher-quality woodchips.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:56.480
Perhaps mahogany? Ooh, that’d be real nice…

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:01.040
Gustavo Abate said, “If you put 2 or&nbsp;
more things, would they fuse into one?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.400
If they do, would the machine separate&nbsp;
them back if programmed right?”

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.440
I don’t believe that SCP-914 would fuse&nbsp;
multiple items or entities that are placed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.560
into its chamber, you may be confusing that&nbsp;
with another anomalous technology - like, say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:21.040
a teleporter. But if a researcher is willing to&nbsp;
step into SCP-914 with a fly, then we might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:26.400
able to see for ourselves whether we’re right…
Stupid People said, “I think it would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:31.600
interesting to put one of SCP 978’s photos&nbsp;
through the “fine” or “very fine” settings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:37.200
Preferably one with an interesting desire&nbsp;
depicted, like the shy guys desire to not exist.”

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.680
It’s unlikely that even the Clockworks would&nbsp;
have the ability to tangibly change reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:47.520
based on the photographs of the Desire Camera.&nbsp;
However, on the Very Fine setting, the photo will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.160
at the very least, begin to move, and&nbsp;
heck, maybe something will even crawl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:57.680
out. That’s when you’ll really regret&nbsp;
putting any photo of SCP-096 in there…

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:03.520
TheGCGamer YT said, “I would insert a cake or&nbsp;
some other type of food on the very fine setting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:08.400
to see if it would come out as a better version&nbsp;
of that food, like a cupcake into a full cake or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:13.280
better quality ingredients. Maybe it would simply&nbsp;
change the flavour and we’d find out that there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.760
some kind of sentience behind the Clockworks&nbsp;
allowing it to have an opinion on flavours.”

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.440
On the Fine setting, everything you’ve&nbsp;
just described is likely to be correct.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:25.440
On the Very Fine setting, on the other&nbsp;
hand, the cake may grow giant spider legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:30.640
start spewing noxious amnestic fumes, and begin&nbsp;
attacking anyone who isn’t brave enough to eat it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.360
and end its reign of delicious,&nbsp;
well-frosted terror. Happy Birthday…

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:41.920
MouldyDorito said, “What about Y-909 from&nbsp;
SCP-3000 on very fine. Interesting to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:46.720
an improved amnestic effect or perhaps&nbsp;
it changes the substance completely. Also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:50.560
interesting if you put it through on&nbsp;
rough or very rough to see the output,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:54.000
probably just a weak anaesthetic&nbsp;
or perhaps just rat poison.”

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:59.360
On Very Fine, the Y-909 amnestic might become&nbsp;
so powerful that just looking at it will induce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.400
a permanent Alzheimer’s-like state in its&nbsp;
victims, effectively deleting their minds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:09.280
On Rough, it may just break the vials it’s&nbsp;
stored in and spill the liquid everywhere.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:14.000
Darkmega5 said, “I’d print out a meme, put&nbsp;
it in on the fine setting (very fine might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.640
have unforeseen consequences) and post whatever&nbsp;
comes out for massive amounts of Reddit karma.”

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:23.680
It’s an honorable plan. We do it already, in our&nbsp;
own way. Whenever we finish a video, we run it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:29.680
through SCP-914 on Fine, just to make sure it’s&nbsp;
at top quality. And once, we did it on Very Fine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.960
We’ll let you speculate as to what&nbsp;
video that was down in the comments…

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:39.360
Braydo said, “I’m actually kinda interested to&nbsp;
see what would happen if we put Keanu through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:47.840
the machine on very fine. Would it just break?”
Oh, Braydo, how can you improve on perfection?

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:53.040
Solrex the Sun King said, “Put my character&nbsp;
sheet for D&amp;D into it on very fine and just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:58.560
see what happens. Just uh, make sure the alignment&nbsp;
is changed to neutral or better before doing so.”

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:02.960
On Very Fine, it’s likely that SCP-914&nbsp;
would ignore the content of the paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:08.000
and instead mutate the paper itself. Perhaps&nbsp;
it would turn itself into a deadly paper plane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:13.120
flying around and blasting little paper turrets&nbsp;
and air-to-surface missiles at its targets.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:17.840
And that might veer a little more&nbsp;
into “Chaotic Evil” territory.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.840
Davon_gaming said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:24.560
“I feel like putting in one of my model tanks&nbsp;
to see how it looks in the very fine setting…”

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:28.240
It’s unlikely that those model&nbsp;
tanks would remain models for long.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:33.440
They may wind up full-sized, fully autonomous,&nbsp;
and chasing you down the Foundation halls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:39.120
firing lasers and radioactive payloads. They might&nbsp;
even receive air support from the paper plane.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.080
Riley Mushill said, “What happens when&nbsp;
you put water in and set it to Very Fine?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.400
Would it become water from the Fountain of Youth&nbsp;
or would it be the best tasting water ever?”

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.840
On Very Fine, the water may become a&nbsp;
nightmarish, aggressive creature that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:58.800
actively seeks out and destroys its human victims,&nbsp;
like SCP-3280, also known as After The Storm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:03.920
Though if we’re extremely lucky, maybe&nbsp;
life-giving anomalous water is in the cards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:09.360
we just don’t like to be overly optimistic&nbsp;
these days. We’ve been burned too many times…

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:13.920
Wildnite Studios said, “I would input the&nbsp;
tickle monster in it and turn the setting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:19.120
fine allowing the tickle's monster's&nbsp;
power to make SCP 682 docile forever.”

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:23.840
While it’s too much of a risk to ever&nbsp;
try putting SCP-999 into SCP-914,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.760
if things went well, 999 may become so powerful&nbsp;
that we’d never experience sadness or anger on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:34.800
earth again. And after everything we’ve been&nbsp;
through, wouldn’t that be a nice reprieve?

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:39.680
Joey Rohlf said, “I would put in one&nbsp;
of the 05 council on very fine setting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:43.040
Then they would make better choices&nbsp;
because they’re better than before.”

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:45.280
Don’t let them know we said this, but personally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:50.640
we don’t think the members of the O5 Council&nbsp;
should be getting any more anomalous superpowers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.840
Aren’t they ambiguously dangerous&nbsp;
and powerful enough already?

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.760
Dysfunctional Dragonborn said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.760 --> 00:14:01.840
“I’d put an NFT into it on very fine and&nbsp;
hope it turns into something of value.”

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.320
Doing this might make their insidious power grow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:17.440
even stronger. Rather than worthless JPEGS,&nbsp;
they might instead become a rival group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:23.040
The NFT Foundation, which - instead of protecting&nbsp;
humanity from evil - instead decides to display a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:28.560
level of evil that rivals even the malice of the&nbsp;
Scarlet King. It’s really not worth finding out.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:32.400
ChosenMosin said, “I’d put my&nbsp;
resume in, turn it to very fine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:35.520
and see if I can eventually&nbsp;
get hired in my college town.”

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:41.280
This is a high-risk, high-reward move. Putting&nbsp;
your resume in on Very Fine may make it a document&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:46.400
that immediately, anomalously convinces potential&nbsp;
employers that you would be the perfect candidate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.880
It may push things further, and make your&nbsp;
prospective employers obsessed with you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:55.520
They follow you home and watch you through&nbsp;
your windows. They wish to take care of you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:59.360
They wish to be wed to you.&nbsp;
They will never leave you alone.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.840
After all, it was an excellent resume.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:02.880
Swagger said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:07.600
“I think putting Hideo Kojima in the very fine&nbsp;
setting would show something very interesting.”

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:12.560
If you run Kojima through the Clockworks on&nbsp;
Very Fine, he might even be powerful enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:17.600
design and release Silent Hills on his own.&nbsp;
No, we’re still not over that. Is anyone?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:21.840
Hearth Fireheart said, “A titanium&nbsp;
prosthetic arm put in on very fine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:26.320
Predicted result of possible prosthetic arm&nbsp;
with anomolous properties, or an enhanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:31.600
titanium prosthetic that can move exactly like a&nbsp;
regular arm, while granting enhanced strength.”

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:35.680
We’re always down for super-powered&nbsp;
robot arms. Chances are, on Very Fine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:40.640
it might even get shapeshifting or immensely&nbsp;
powerful reality-warping abilities - So powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:46.080
it may even begin to change the rest of your&nbsp;
body. Picture what happens to Tetsuo in Akira.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:49.440
Bunger said, “Put a burger on&nbsp;
the very fine setting I'm very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:52.800
curious as to what would happen to&nbsp;
something as simple as a burger.”

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:57.680
All we’ll say is, we definitely don’t recommend&nbsp;
eating the burger after you’ve run it through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.120
It may wind up eating you from&nbsp;
the inside once you’re done…

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:05.520
Deez said, “I would put raw steak in&nbsp;
the machine and put it on “Very Fine”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.800
that way the steak will taste&nbsp;
very delicious and be very fine.”

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:16.000
I’m beginning to sense that people were just&nbsp;
getting hungry when they started sending these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:21.200
ones in. And we definitely don’t think&nbsp;
you should put a steak into SCP-914.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.440
For all we know, it might turn it&nbsp;
into SCP-058 and get us all killed.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:30.960
Nicholas Lau said, “Alright, this'll sound&nbsp;
disgusting. I toss in a jar some of my own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:36.000
toenails, hair, dandruff, spit and&nbsp;
tears. Then, cover the jar in lead paint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.720
put on a sticker saying "WARNING: RADIOACTIVE&nbsp;
MATERIALS" and come in with a hazmat suit and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:45.200
a lead shield. Put on Fine, then evacuate&nbsp;
the room for the object to appear.”

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:55.040
Well, that’s one of the most revolting answers&nbsp;
we’ve ever received here on SCP Explained.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:59.440
Well done, Nicholas. It’s going to be a while&nbsp;
until we can get this thought out of our heads.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:02.000
This is the exact opposite of “Very Fine.”

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.840
Ray Parenteau said, “A&nbsp;
Nickelback CD on Very Fine.”

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.840
Just like we said for Keanu earlier,&nbsp;
how could you improve on perfection?

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.840
And there you have it, folks. Thanks again&nbsp;
to everyone who sent in their fascinating and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:23.920
disturbing answers. If you want to be in the next&nbsp;
video like this, keep an eye on our community tab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:28.720
And thank you for your continued support&nbsp;
- You’ll always be Very Fine to us.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:33.200
Now go check out “How To Actually&nbsp;
Beat SCP-3008 The Infinite Ikea”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:38.560
and “SCP-096 - Look at a Picture of Shy Guy&nbsp;
in Space? The Shy Guy Questions and Theories”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:43.920
for more of the weirdest and wildest&nbsp;
responses from the SCP Explained community!

